{#
  One field, rendered once, with the error state nothing used to enter.

  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  WHY THESE ARE MACROS AND NOT COPIED MARKUP
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  `.ag-field[data-invalid]` and `.ag-err` have been in `components.css` since the
  design system landed. The only place in the whole tree that set `data-invalid` was
  `dev-ui.twig` — the style gallery. So the error state existed as a swatch on a demo
  page and was entered by no form anybody fills in. That is this codebase's §17 at the
  view layer: a declaration with no reader, which the next person copies in good faith
  because it looks like the convention.

  The ARIA wiring is the reason it has to be one place rather than a pattern people
  remember. A field in error owes FOUR things that have to agree with each other:

    · `aria-invalid="true"` on the control, not on the wrapper — assistive technology
      reads the control.
    · `aria-describedby` naming BOTH the hint and the error, in that order, because a
      person who has just been told "that is not a valid date" needs the format
      immediately afterwards, not before.
    · an id on each of those that is unique on the page.
    · the message as TEXT, never as a colour or an icon alone (WCAG 1.4.1).

  Hand-written four times, those agree three times.

  ── THE HINT IS NOT A PLACEHOLDER ──────────────────────────────────────────────

  A rule stated only in a `placeholder` is stated to nobody: it vanishes the moment
  somebody types, so the only person who ever saw it had not started, and the only one
  who needed it had. This codebase shipped exactly that with an eight-character
  password minimum. `hint` renders as text that stays.

  ── AND `novalidate` IS ON THE FORM, DELIBERATELY ──────────────────────────────

  The browser's own bubble is untranslated, unstyled, dismissed on the next keystroke,
  and says something the server may not agree with. `form_open()` sets `novalidate`
  and the `required`/`minlength` attributes stay — they still carry the rule to
  assistive technology and to the client-side check, they just no longer open a bubble
  this site cannot write.
#}

{# ── the error summary, which is the part a screen reader needs ──────────────── #}
{#
  WCAG 3.3.1 asks for the item in error to be IDENTIFIED. A banner reading "Please
  check the form" identifies nothing, and on an eleven-field nomination it is an
  instruction to go hunting. This lists each failure as a link to the field.

  It takes focus on render (`tabindex="-1"` plus the script), so somebody arriving
  back at the page is told what happened instead of starting again at the top. It is
  `role="alert"` so it is announced even when focus does not move.
#}
{% macro summary(errors, message, labels) %}
  {% if errors|length or message %}
    <div class="ag-formsum" role="alert" tabindex="-1" data-ag-form-summary>
      <p class="ag-formsum__t">
        {%- if errors|length == 1 -%}
          There is one thing to fix
        {%- elseif errors|length -%}
          There are {{ errors|length }} things to fix
        {%- else -%}
          We could not save that
        {%- endif -%}
      </p>
      {% if message %}<p class="ag-formsum__m">{{ message }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if errors|length %}
        <ul class="ag-formsum__list">
          {% for field, text in errors %}
            <li><a href="#f-{{ field }}">{{ labels[field]|default(text) == text ? text : labels[field] ~ ': ' ~ text }}</a></li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}

{#
  A text-like control: text, email, tel, url, number, password, date.

  `opts` carries everything optional so a caller never has to pass nine positional
  arguments: hint, required, type, value, autocomplete, inputmode, minlength,
  maxlength, pattern, placeholder, suffix.
#}
{% macro text(name, label, errors, old, opts) %}
  {% set o = opts|default({}) %}
  {% set err = errors[name]|default('') %}
  {% set id = 'f-' ~ name %}
  {% set hint = o.hint|default('') %}
  {#
    Both ids are named whether or not they render, then filtered — a describedby
    pointing at an element that is not on the page is read as nothing by some screen
    readers and as the literal id by others.
  #}
  {% set described = [hint ? id ~ '-hint' : '', err ? id ~ '-err' : '']|filter(v => v)|join(' ') %}

  <div class="ag-fieldset">
    <label class="ag-label" for="{{ id }}">
      {{ label }}
      {% if o.required|default(false) %}
        <span class="ag-label__req" aria-hidden="true">*</span><span class="ag-sr">(required)</span>
      {% else %}
        <span class="ag-label__opt">Optional</span>
      {% endif %}
    </label>

    {% if hint %}<p class="ag-hint" id="{{ id }}-hint">{{ hint }}</p>{% endif %}

    <span class="ag-field"{% if err %} data-invalid{% endif %}>
      <input
        type="{{ o.type|default('text') }}"
        id="{{ id }}" name="{{ name }}"
        value="{{ old[name]|default(o.value|default('')) }}"
        {% if o.required|default(false) %}required{% endif %}
        {% if o.autocomplete|default('') %}autocomplete="{{ o.autocomplete }}"{% endif %}
        {% if o.inputmode|default('') %}inputmode="{{ o.inputmode }}"{% endif %}
        {% if o.minlength|default(0) %}minlength="{{ o.minlength }}"{% endif %}
        {% if o.maxlength|default(0) %}maxlength="{{ o.maxlength }}"{% endif %}
        {% if o.pattern|default('') %}pattern="{{ o.pattern }}"{% endif %}
        {% if o.placeholder|default('') %}placeholder="{{ o.placeholder }}"{% endif %}
        {% if err %}aria-invalid="true"{% endif %}
        {% if described %}aria-describedby="{{ described }}"{% endif %}>
      {% if o.suffix|default('') %}<span class="ag-field__suffix">{{ o.suffix }}</span>{% endif %}
    </span>

    {{ _self.message(id, err) }}
  </div>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro textarea(name, label, errors, old, opts) %}
  {% set o = opts|default({}) %}
  {% set err = errors[name]|default('') %}
  {% set id = 'f-' ~ name %}
  {% set hint = o.hint|default('') %}
  {% set described = [hint ? id ~ '-hint' : '', err ? id ~ '-err' : '', o.counter|default(false) ? id ~ '-count' : '']|filter(v => v)|join(' ') %}

  <div class="ag-fieldset">
    <label class="ag-label" for="{{ id }}">
      {{ label }}
      {% if o.required|default(false) %}
        <span class="ag-label__req" aria-hidden="true">*</span><span class="ag-sr">(required)</span>
      {% else %}
        <span class="ag-label__opt">Optional</span>
      {% endif %}
    </label>

    {% if hint %}<p class="ag-hint" id="{{ id }}-hint">{{ hint }}</p>{% endif %}

    <textarea
      class="ag-field" id="{{ id }}" name="{{ name }}"
      {% if err %}data-invalid aria-invalid="true"{% endif %}
      {% if o.required|default(false) %}required{% endif %}
      {% if o.minlength|default(0) %}minlength="{{ o.minlength }}"{% endif %}
      {% if o.maxlength|default(0) %}maxlength="{{ o.maxlength }}"{% endif %}
      {% if o.rows|default(0) %}rows="{{ o.rows }}"{% endif %}
      {% if described %}aria-describedby="{{ described }}"{% endif %}>{{ old[name]|default(o.value|default('')) }}</textarea>

    {#
      A live counter is announced POLITELY and only near the limit. `aria-live` on a
      counter that speaks every keystroke makes the field unusable with a screen
      reader — the characters are read back over the person's own typing.
    #}
    {% if o.counter|default(false) %}
      <p class="ag-count" id="{{ id }}-count" data-ag-count="{{ o.minlength|default(0) }}"
         data-ag-max="{{ o.maxlength|default(0) }}" aria-live="polite"></p>
    {% endif %}

    {{ _self.message(id, err) }}
  </div>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro select(name, label, options, errors, old, opts) %}
  {% set o = opts|default({}) %}
  {% set err = errors[name]|default('') %}
  {% set id = 'f-' ~ name %}
  {% set hint = o.hint|default('') %}
  {% set described = [hint ? id ~ '-hint' : '', err ? id ~ '-err' : '']|filter(v => v)|join(' ') %}
  {% set chosen = old[name]|default(o.value|default('')) %}

  <div class="ag-fieldset">
    <label class="ag-label" for="{{ id }}">
      {{ label }}
      {% if o.required|default(false) %}
        <span class="ag-label__req" aria-hidden="true">*</span><span class="ag-sr">(required)</span>
      {% else %}
        <span class="ag-label__opt">Optional</span>
      {% endif %}
    </label>

    {% if hint %}<p class="ag-hint" id="{{ id }}-hint">{{ hint }}</p>{% endif %}

    <span class="ag-field"{% if err %} data-invalid{% endif %}>
      <select id="{{ id }}" name="{{ name }}"
        {% if o.required|default(false) %}required{% endif %}
        {% if err %}aria-invalid="true"{% endif %}
        {% if described %}aria-describedby="{{ described }}"{% endif %}>
        {% if o.blank|default('') %}<option value="">{{ o.blank }}</option>{% endif %}
        {% for value, text in options %}
          <option value="{{ value }}"{{ chosen == value ? ' selected' : '' }}>{{ text }}</option>
        {% endfor %}
      </select>
    </span>

    {{ _self.message(id, err) }}
  </div>
{% endmacro %}

{#
  The message itself, and the reason it is one macro.

  The icon is `aria-hidden` and the sentence carries the meaning, because colour and
  shape alone fail 1.4.1 — and the error red here is `--ag-error` on paper, which a
  person with low vision may read as ordinary text.
#}
{% macro message(id, err) %}
  {% if err %}
    <p class="ag-err" id="{{ id }}-err">
      <svg class="ag-err__i" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
           stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v6M12 16.5v.5"/>
      </svg>
      {{ err }}
    </p>
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
